WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.503 --> 00:00:01.920
MANDAR JOG: Hi,
my name is Mandar,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.710
and I lead the extensibility
team for Istio at Google.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.320
We recently gave a talk about
adding fine-grained mesh

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.360
telemetry to the service mesh.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.590
When we moved from a monolith
to a microservices world,

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.575
we replaced an
in-memory function call

00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:18.870
with the Remote RPC.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.490
That essentially
replaced something

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.790
that was fast, reliable,
and secure with something

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.820
that was not as fast, not as
reliable, and not as secure.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.560
Service mesh tries to
impart these qualities back

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.620
into the microservices world.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.700
Istio uses Envoy as the
basis of its service mesh.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.030
And Envoy has some fairly
good stats collection already.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.590
However, one part that it
lacks is peer awareness.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.890
Knowing [INAUDIBLE]
is extremely important

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.770
when you're talking
about microservices.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.730
As part of this work, we
have added metadata exchange

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.770
as a standard part of HTTP flow.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.210
Luckily, every pair of
communicating proxies

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.550
know who they are talking with.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:09.870
We have also added
WebAssembly support to Envoy

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.660
as part of this
effort, which is going

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.040
to help the entire community.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.480
All this work is available.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.210
And it's still 1.4,
so you can try it out.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.940
And the underpinnings are
available in the Envoy/WASM

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.280
repository in the Envoy org.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.490
Please come by our
booth at Google,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.570
and thanks for listening.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.320
[MUSIC PLAYING]

